  "description": {
    "de": "This report covers the results for projections of the air pollutants SO2, NOx, non-methane NMVOC, NH3 and particulate matter (PM2.5) under the scenarios “with existing measures” (WEM) and “with additional measures” (WAM). It updates the previous projections for air pollutants published in 2021 (REP-0769).  The scenarios WEM and WAM results in significant emission reductions from 2005 to 2030 for all pollutants. The most substantial reduction, about 67% for WEM and about 69% for WAM, is projected for the pollutant NOx. Emission reductions for the other pollutants range from 8% to 56% in the scenario WEM and from 18% to 60% in the scenario WAM."
  },
